#: admin/healthcheck.php:125
msgid "OpenPorte replay protection:"
msgstr ""

#: admin/healthcheck.php:153
msgid "Expiration is set to 0, so a solved challenge never expires and only Replay limit bounds how often it can be resubmitted. This is strongly discouraged and is being evaluated for deprecation — set an expiry of 60 seconds or more."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %d is the configured Expiration value, in seconds
#: admin/healthcheck.php:161
#, php-format
msgid "Expiration is set to %d seconds, which can elapse before a slow device finishes solving the challenge and turn legitimate submissions into failures. Values below 60 seconds are being evaluated for deprecation."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s is a duration such as "5 mins"
#: admin/healthcheck.php:194
#, php-format
msgid "Submissions were accepted without being counted in the last %s, because the reuse counter could not be stored. Protection degrades to accepting valid challenges unconditionally while that lasts — check the persistent object cache or the database."
msgstr ""

#: admin/healthcheck.php:203
msgid "Replay limit is 0, so replay protection is off: a solved challenge is accepted for as long as it stays valid, however many times it is submitted. This is the behaviour of releases before 1.29.0."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %1$d is the configured Replay limit, %2$s names where the counter is stored
#: admin/healthcheck.php:211
#, php-format
msgid "Each solved challenge is accepted %1$d time, counted in %2$s."
msgid_plural "Each solved challenge is accepted up to %1$d times, counted in %2$s."
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""

#: admin/healthcheck.php:219
msgid "the persistent object cache"
msgstr ""

#: admin/healthcheck.php:220
msgid "the database"
msgstr ""

#: admin/healthcheck.php:238
msgid "API mode is Custom but no Challenge URL is configured."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s is the connection error message
#: admin/healthcheck.php:280
#, php-format
msgid "The Challenge URL is unreachable: %s"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %d is the HTTP status code returned by the backend
#: admin/healthcheck.php:291
#, php-format
msgid "The Challenge URL responded with HTTP %d instead of a challenge. Check the URL (including any apiKey parameter) and the backend's domain/origin restrictions."
msgstr ""

#: admin/healthcheck.php:301
msgid "The Challenge URL did not return an ALTCHA challenge (JSON with algorithm, challenge, salt and signature fields expected)."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s is the algorithm name reported by the backend
#: admin/healthcheck.php:310
#, php-format
msgid "The backend issues challenges with the unsupported algorithm \"%s\"."
msgstr ""

#: admin/healthcheck.php:326
msgid "The shared secret does not match the backend's HMAC secret — every form submission would fail verification. Copy the backend's HMAC secret into the Signing secret field."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %1$s is the algorithm used by the backend, %2$s the algorithm configured in OpenPorte
#: admin/healthcheck.php:334
#, php-format
msgid "The backend issues %1$s challenges but the Algorithm setting is %2$s — form submissions would fail verification. Set Algorithm to %1$s."
msgstr ""

#: admin/healthcheck.php:348
msgid "The backend issues challenges with no expiry (no future \"expires\" parameter in the salt), so a solved challenge never expires on its own and only Replay limit bounds how often it is accepted. Enable challenge expiry on the backend."
msgstr ""

#: admin/healthcheck.php:354
msgid "The backend returned a challenge whose expiry is already in the past. Its clock may be wrong or it may be serving a cached challenge; correct that before using Custom mode."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s is the algorithm confirmed with the backend
#: admin/healthcheck.php:359
#, php-format
msgid "The Challenge URL responds with a valid %s challenge and the shared secret matches."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s is a duration such as "20 mins"
#: admin/healthcheck.php:364
#, php-format
msgid "The backend expires its challenges after about %s."
msgstr ""

#: admin/healthcheck.php:368
msgid "That is short enough to expire before a slow device finishes solving, which turns legitimate submissions into failures."
msgstr ""

