msgstr ""

#: includes/settings.php:281
msgid "Self-hosted"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings.php:291
msgid "Challenge URL"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings.php:299
msgid "Only available when API Mode is set to Custom.<br/>The URL is made up of the domain and path to your <strong>custom ALTCHA-compatible backend</strong>, and optionally an API key (it starts with <code>gk_</code>)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings.php:308
msgid "Shared secret"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings.php:316
msgid "A secret key used to sign and verify challenges."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings.php:319
msgid "OpenPorte generates a random secret automatically. Change it only if another application needs to use the same secret.<br/>In Custom API Mode, this value <strong>must exactly match</strong> the shared secret (sometimes called the HMAC secret) configured in your backend."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings.php:321
msgid "Copy places the current secret on the clipboard. Regenerate fills in a fresh random secret; it only takes effect when you save changes, and challenges already issued with the old secret then stop verifying. In Custom API Mode, saving a new secret also breaks verification of new submissions until you update the secret on your backend to match."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings.php:331
#: includes/settings.php:337
msgid "Hash algorithm for the challenges."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings.php:331
msgid "Algorithm"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings.php:338
msgid "In Self-hosted API Mode this is the algorithm used to generate and verify the proof-of-work challenges.<br/>In Custom API Mode it must match the algorithm your backend uses — most ALTCHA-compatible backends default to SHA-256."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings.php:348
msgid "Low"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings.php:349
msgid "Medium"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings.php:350
msgid "High"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings.php:360
msgid "Complexity"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings.php:370
msgid "Disabled in Custom mode: the backend sets the challenge complexity."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings.php:371
msgid "Select the PoW complexity for the widget: the higher the complexity, the longer visitors (and bots) work to solve the challenge.<br/>Even High is usually solved in under a second on a recent computer; on older phones it can take a few seconds. High is roughly 2–3× the work of Low."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings.php:378
msgid "Expiration"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings.php:389
msgid "Disabled in Custom mode: the backend sets the challenge expiry."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings.php:392
msgid "Life-span of a challenge. Custom accepts 0 to 14400 seconds, where 0 means no expiry and 14400 is 4 hours."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings.php:394
msgid "Above 300 seconds the window in which a solved challenge can be replayed grows, though Replay limit still bounds how often one is accepted. Below 60 seconds a challenge can expire before a slow device finishes solving it, and 0 means it never expires at all — both are discouraged and are being evaluated for deprecation."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings.php:400
msgid "Replay limit"
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings.php:406
msgid "How many times one solved challenge may be accepted. This applies in both API Modes."
msgstr ""

#: includes/settings.php:408
msgid "A visitor whose form comes back with an unrelated error (a missing field, a mistyped password) resubmits the same challenge, so a small allowance keeps those submissions working; every extra use is also one more replay available to a bot. Custom accepts 0 to 100, where 0 accepts a solved challenge for as long as it is valid — the behaviour of releases before 1.29.0, and not recommended."
msgstr ""

